ALL RIGHTS RESERVED — PROPRIETARY COMMERCIAL SOFTWARE.

1. Scope and Covered Proprietary Modules
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Pro and Enterprise editions of PhasorWave (collectively, the "Commercial
Software") are proprietary commercial software owned exclusively by PhasorWave
DeepTech Systems ("Licensor", https://phasorwave.dev) and are NOT covered by
AGPLv3 or MIT. The Commercial Software includes, without limitation:
  - Full ITU-R P.618-14 rain attenuation kernels (`ITU_P618_RainModel`) [Pro+]
  - Dynamic Hufnagel-Valley (HV-5/7) optical atmospheric turbulence kernels
    (`OpticalTurbulence_HV57`) [Enterprise Exclusive]
  - High-order Generalized Memory Polynomial (GMP) DPD modeling and two-pass
    DGKS QR Indirect Learning Architecture (`DPD_GMP_Model`) [Enterprise Exclusive]
  - GNU Radio 4.0 Out-of-Tree plugin blocks (`gr-phasorwave`:
    `itu_p618_channel`, `optical_hv57_channel`, `dpd_gmp_extract`,
    `dpd_gmp_apply`) [Pro / Enterprise]
  - Compiled binary distributions, extensions, and shared libraries (`.pyd`,
    `.so`, `.whl`, `libphasorwave_core.so`, and unlocked C++23 SIMD execution
    engines)
  - Offline Ed25519 cryptographic license enforcement (`phy::LicenseGuard`) and
    the Cloudflare Worker / KMS licensing infrastructure (`licensing/`)

2. License Grant, Cryptographic Activation, and Restrictions
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Subject to timely payment of all applicable license fees and continuous
compliance with this EULA, Licensor grants the purchasing entity or individual
("Licensee") a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable,
revocable license to install and execute the Commercial Software strictly
within the authorized tier (Pro or Enterprise), seat/deployment scope, and
term specified in the applicable order and `.lic` token.

Execution of Pro and Enterprise modules requires a valid, unexpired, and
unrevoked `.lic` token cryptographically signed with PhasorWave's Ed25519
private key and verified offline against the embedded public key
(`kPhasorWavePublicKey`).

Unauthorized reproduction, distribution, decompilation, disassembly, reverse
engineering, removal or circumvention of `LicenseGuard` checks, or
redistribution of source distributions (`sdist`) or unlocked WASM benchmark
binaries outside their authorized evaluation scope is strictly prohibited
without a separate written commercial license agreement from PhasorWave
DeepTech Systems (https://phasorwave.dev | licenses@phasorwave.dev).

